// Deal or Force - every country by its tag.
//
// `CountryNames.Resolve` asks for `country.<TAG>.name` before it asks for anything else,
// so this is where a country's name lives and 20_countries.json is the fallback nobody
// reaches any more. Three letters mean one country; an English sentence means whatever
// else in the game happens to be spelled the same way, which is how the language picker
// once offered the English PEOPLE as a language.
//
// Generated from common/countries. A country renamed there keeps its translation,
// which is the whole point of keying by tag.
//
// A government- or ideology-specific name is a longer key and is authored by hand:
//   country.RUS.government.republic.name, country.RUS.map, formable.<id>.name
